    intro="Research project management is the planning and control of research work, such as a funded grant, a multi-partner consortium or a corporate R&D programme, so that it meets funder rules, budgets and deadlines while leaving room for results nobody can predict. This guide covers how research projects differ, who does what, the life cycle, a 12-step process and a worked grant example with milestones, budget and a mid-project review.",
